      {
        "id": "load-length-and-rigidity",
        "kind": "explain",
        "blocks": [],
        "headline": "Tip deflection is the load times the length cubed, over three times EI.",
        "lead": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "A cantilever loaded at its tip bends by δ = PL³/3EI. E and I together, EI, are the flexural rigidity: material stiffness times section shape. Work in base units: newtons, metres, pascals and m⁴. 1 GPa is 10⁹ Pa, and 10⁶ mm⁴ is 10⁻⁶ m⁴."
          }
        ],
        "reveal": [],
        "introducesTerms": [
          "flexural rigidity"
        ],
        "visualStateId": "",
        "checkQuestionId": "engr-deflection-and-stiffness-8",
        "activityId": ""
      },
      {
